{#- RB4011 — HD-312 guest turn-up + IOT-WAN/Kids removal DELTA (2026-09-03).
    Live CRITICAL delta applied via /import — idempotent (:if-find guards, safe to re-import).
    Targets: RB4011 CAPsMAN manager only.
    Owner decision 2026-09-03: turn up 'Kogler guest' (VLAN 30, 5GHz-only), DELETE the
    'Kogler IOT WAN' (VLAN 21) and 'Kogler Kids' (VLAN 40) SSID configurations.
    SSOT: group_vars/router.yml routeros_capsman_ssids (+ band: 5 for guest).
    NOTE: NO secrets — passphrases already live in the security profiles from the
    steady-state render; this delta only toggles configs + provisioning.
    Apply: /import rb4011_guest_delta.rsc
    Companion deltas: crs328_guest_delta.rsc (switch AP-port VLAN 30) +
    ap_guest_delta.rsc (per-AP bridge VLAN 30 post-provision). -#}
# =============================================================================
# HD-312 guest turn-up + IOT-WAN/Kids removal — RB4011 CAPsMAN DELTA
# =============================================================================

# ---- 1. Enable the guest wifi config (cfg-kogler-guest: VLAN 30, 5GHz) ----
:if ([/interface wifi configuration find where name=cfg-kogler-guest] != "") do={
    /interface wifi configuration set [find where name=cfg-kogler-guest] disabled=no
} else={
    :error "HD-312 delta: cfg-kogler-guest missing — steady-state rsc not imported?"
}

# ---- 2. DELETE the IOT-WAN + Kids SSID configurations ----
# (config objects first — the profiles below are removed once nothing references them)
:if ([/interface wifi configuration find where name=cfg-kogler-iot-wan] != "") do={
    /interface wifi configuration remove [find where name=cfg-kogler-iot-wan]
}
:if ([/interface wifi configuration find where name=cfg-kogler-kids] != "") do={
    /interface wifi configuration remove [find where name=cfg-kogler-kids]
}

# ---- 3. DELETE the IOT-WAN + Kids security profiles (no longer referenced) ----
:if ([/interface wifi security find where name=sec-kogler-iot-wan] != "") do={
    /interface wifi security remove [find where name=sec-kogler-iot-wan]
}
:if ([/interface wifi security find where name=sec-kogler-kids] != "") do={
    /interface wifi security remove [find where name=sec-kogler-kids]
}

# ---- 4. Add guest to the 5GHz provisioning (master cfg-kogler-5) ----
# The 5GHz master already exists (cfg-kogler-5, ch36 non-DFS). Extend its slave list
# with cfg-kogler-guest. NOTE (live 2026-09-03): `get slave-configurations` returns nil
# on the 5GHz rule, so the idempotent read-check is unreliable — a plain `set` is safe
# (re-setting the same slave is a no-op on RouterOS 7.24).
:local fiveGHz [/interface wifi provisioning find where master-configuration=cfg-kogler-5]
:if ($fiveGHz != "") do={
    /interface wifi provisioning set $fiveGHz slave-configurations=cfg-kogler-guest
} else={
    :error "HD-312 delta: 5GHz provisioning rule (master=cfg-kogler-5) missing"
}

# ---- 5. CAP re-provision kick (the 5GHz slave materializes at the CAP) ----
# Without this, the guest slave may not appear on the CAP despite slaves-static=yes
# (live-verified 2026-09-03: guest slave only materialized after the CAP reloaded).
/interface wifi capsman set enabled=no
/interface wifi capsman set enabled=yes

# ---- End ----
# Verify:
#   /interface wifi configuration print   -> cfg-kogler-guest enabled, iot-wan/kids gone
#   /interface wifi security print        -> sec-kogler-guest present, iot-wan/kids gone
#   /interface wifi provisioning print    -> 5GHz rule now has slave cfg-kogler-guest
#   AP: /interface wifi print             -> 'Kogler guest' slave present
#   AP: /interface bridge vlan print      -> VLAN 30 tagged ether1 untagged <guest slave>